            }
        }
    }
}
What happens?

Suppose:

Build #1 starts
Build #2 starts shortly after

Both builds enter the Build stage.

The newer build reaches the later milestone first.

The milestone mechanism prevents an older build from proceeding past a milestone when a newer build has already passed that milestone.

Therefore, the older overlapping build can be aborted at the milestone, while the newer build continues.

Why milestone(1)?
milestone(1)

prevents an outdated build from continuing into later pipeline work after a newer build has progressed beyond that point.

Why milestone(2)?
stage('Deploy') {
    steps {
        milestone(2)
        ...
    }
}

This gives additional protection at the entrance to Deploy.

It helps prevent an older build from reaching deployment after a newer build has already passed that deployment milestone.

